Hyundai Elantra today?"

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:30.767
First thing he'll do
in the office --

00:10:30.767 --> 00:10:32.367
Even out his spray tan.

00:10:32.367 --> 00:10:34.968
[ Applause ]

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:36.467
Then we have Robert Newman.

00:10:36.467 --> 00:10:38.000
Job -- Farmer.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.467
Currently --
FaceTiming his grandchildren

00:10:40.467 --> 00:10:42.400
too close to the camera.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.100
Last seen --
as a signed head shot

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.000
on the wall
of an Italian restaurant.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.534
[ Applause ]

00:10:48.534 --> 00:10:50.434
And, finally, it's David Moore.

00:10:50.434 --> 00:10:51.868
Job -- Teacher.

00:10:51.868 --> 00:10:54.300
Last person he upset --
His barber.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:58.434
Catalogue model for --
Clip-on ties.

00:10:58.434 --> 00:11:00.667
Campaign slogan --
"Don't call them comic books,

00:11:00.667 --> 00:11:02.734
they're graphic novels."

00:11:02.734 --> 00:11:05.801
This has been "Fast Stats,"
everybody.

00:11:05.801 --> 00:11:07.434
Thank you very much.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:12.734
Hey, we had some shocking --
some sad news today.

00:11:12.734 --> 00:11:15.801
It was told to us that
Norm Macdonald,

00:11:15.801 --> 00:11:20.167
a great comedian, passed away
today at the age of 61.

00:11:20.167 --> 00:11:22.033
And, gosh, you know him.

00:11:22.033 --> 00:11:23.334
You love him.
-Yeah.

00:11:23.334 --> 00:11:26.200
-And he's just one of
the greatest comedians ever,

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.801
and, God,
we're going to miss him.

00:11:27.801 --> 00:11:30.634
He was a friend of the show --
family, really, to us.

00:11:30.634 --> 00:11:31.934
We've known him forever.

00:11:31.934 --> 00:11:35.400
I remember Norm -- I would do
impressions of Norm.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.968
In like the late '80s, I would
videotape every comedian.

00:11:38.968 --> 00:11:40.968
They had all these comedy shows
on all the time.

00:11:40.968 --> 00:11:44.467
Like, it was on every channel,
and I would know everyone's act.

00:11:44.467 --> 00:11:47.934
Judy Tenuta, Jann Karam.

00:11:47.934 --> 00:11:49.267
Everyone's act I would know.

00:11:49.267 --> 00:11:51.534
And this guy comes on,
Norm Macdonald.

00:11:51.534 --> 00:11:54.667
This guy -- "Hey, crazy accent."

00:11:54.667 --> 00:11:59.100
And he's so funny and he was so
cool-looking and so confident.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.467
And he told this bit about
a wiener dog.

00:12:01.467 --> 00:12:02.534
I don't know if
you know this bit.

00:12:02.534 --> 00:12:04.734
He's like, "Hey,
he's trying to get a dog,

00:12:04.734 --> 00:12:06.300
you know, at the dog market.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.634
It's crazy, the dog market.

00:12:08.634 --> 00:12:10.400
It's really expensive
to buy a dog, you know?

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:13.934
I'm not telling you anything
you don't know.

00:12:13.934 --> 00:12:15.667
Dog market --
A lot of money for a dog.

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:18.968
You know, you pay like 500 bucks
for a dog.

00:12:18.968 --> 00:12:20.601
You know, I was thinking,
if I was to get a dog,

00:12:20.601 --> 00:12:24.734
it'd probably be maybe
like 1 buck,

00:12:24.734 --> 00:12:27.501
maybe 2 bucks max,
you know, for a dog.

00:12:27.501 --> 00:12:28.834
You know, they go,
"Oh, you got to get this dog.

00:12:28.834 --> 00:12:31.734
You get a, uh, pit bull.

00:12:31.734 --> 00:12:33.067
You get a pit-bull dog.

00:12:33.067 --> 00:12:36.467
You know, it's 500 bucks
for a pit-bull dog.

00:12:36.467 --> 00:12:40.100
If you get a pit bull, it will
take care of your valuables.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:43.300
Do I look like
I own any valuables?

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.601
If I get a pit bull,
probably the most valuable thing

00:12:45.601 --> 00:12:48.501
I'll own is the pit bull.

00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:51.834
Then you got to get another dog
to take care of the pit bull.

00:12:51.834 --> 00:12:54.200
When I was growing up,
you know, we had a Dober-man.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.801
That was the most dangerous dog.

00:12:56.801 --> 00:12:59.200
Dober-man was
the most dangerous dog.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:03.801
It'd rip your throat out,
you get a Dober-man.

00:13:03.801 --> 00:13:07.701
Yeah, if I want a dog,
I want a dog I can take out.

00:13:07.701 --> 00:13:09.501
I want a dog
that won't mess with you.

00:13:09.501 --> 00:13:13.300
You know, if I get a dog,
I'd get, like, a wiener dog.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:14.734
A wiener dog
won't rip your throat out.

00:13:14.734 --> 00:13:17.467
You know,
unless you're maybe, like,

00:13:17.467 --> 00:13:20.434
laying on the ground
sleeping or something.

00:13:20.434 --> 00:13:22.534
Wiener dog come over and start
nibbling on your throat.

00:13:22.534 --> 00:13:27.467
You know, you wake up, 'Hey, get
out of here, you wiener dog!

00:13:27.467 --> 00:13:31.334
Who do you think you are,
a pit bull?'"

00:13:31.334 --> 00:13:33.267
Anyways, that was
one of the bits.

00:13:33.267 --> 00:13:36.200
I memorized his whole act.
I loved him.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:38.167
And then I got --
Obviously, "Weekend Update,"

00:13:38.167 --> 00:13:40.634
he changed the whole game.

00:13:40.634 --> 00:13:42.868
And I remember just getting on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:13:42.868 --> 00:13:45.634
And I was in L.A.
and I went to some hotel.

00:13:45.634 --> 00:13:48.701
And I'm walking past the lobby,
and who's having breakfast?

00:13:48.701 --> 00:13:50.334
Norm Macdonald.
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:13:50.334 --> 00:13:51.601
So I go over.

00:13:51.601 --> 00:13:55.634
I'm freaking out, 'cause
he's one of my comedy idols.

00:13:55.634 --> 00:13:57.133
And I go over to him --
I go, "Oh, Norm --"

00:13:57.133 --> 00:13:58.300
I go, "Hi.

00:13:58.300 --> 00:13:59.334
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:13:59.334 --> 00:14:03.367
I just love you so much.
You're the best."

00:14:03.367 --> 00:14:06.801
And he was eating breakfast
with Bob Newhart,

00:14:06.801 --> 00:14:09.434
and he looked at me he goes,
"The best?"

00:14:09.434 --> 00:14:11.434
[ Laughter ]

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:16.000
"This is Bob Newhart.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.834
I go, "I didn't know it was
Bob Newhart that --

00:14:18.834 --> 00:14:21.834
I didn't know you were
eating breakfast with Bob.

00:14:21.834 --> 00:14:24.000
Yes, you are the best.
Sorry, Mr. Newhart.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.734
You actually are the best,
but, Norm, you are --"

00:14:25.734 --> 00:14:28.067
You know, it's like --
But that's so --

00:14:28.067 --> 00:14:29.601
He didn't want him
to just take the thing

00:14:29.601 --> 00:14:30.601
that he was the best.

00:14:30.601 --> 00:14:32.701
But he was a comic's comic,

00:14:32.701 --> 00:14:36.133
and everyone absolutely
loved him, top to bottom.

00:14:36.133 --> 00:14:39.667
And he will be missed.

00:14:39.667 --> 00:14:40.734
Yeah.

